# best.rule — a compact, high-yield ruleset for a first pass.
#
# Authored for Hashsmith rather than copied from another project, and kept
# deliberately small: every rule here multiplies the wordlist, so a first pass
# wants the transformations that recover the most passwords per unit of work,
# not every transformation that exists. Run a larger set afterwards if this one
# comes up empty.
#
# Order is roughly by yield: the identity and case changes first, then the
# appended digits and symbols that dominate real password policies, then
# duplication and reversal.
